  <main_text>
    <p><i>Procul, procul facessite</i></p>
    <p><i>Nam me licet sciam graues</i></p>
    <p><i>Patrasse culpas, me tamen</i></p>
    <p><i>Pax alma Christi recreat,</i></p>
    <p><i>Pressumque pectus erigit.</i></p>
    <p><i>Telluris infima loca</i></p>
    <p><i>Valete tandem, nunc domos</i></p>
    <p><i>Scando supernas. Accipe</i></p>
    <p><i>Hoc terra corpus, arbitri</i></p>
    <p><i>Donec supremi legibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Certis refurgant mortui.</i></p>
    <p><i>Valete rura Gallia,</i></p>
    <p><i>Quae me parentis egredi.</i></p>
    <p><i>Vidistis alno Infantulum</i></p>
    <p><i>Prima, &amp; tenellum parvulis</i></p>
    <p><i>Vagire cunis, &amp; mea</i></p>
    <p><i>Nutricis ubera fugere.</i></p>
    <p><i>O dulcis olim patria</i></p>
    <p><i>Terras relinquo te procul</i></p>
    <p><i>Lubens, quod impias fores</i></p>
    <p><i>Sinu cohortes, quae tua</i></p>
    <p><i>Per arua gaudent sanguinem</i></p>
    <p><i>Gregis piorum fundere.</i></p>
    <p><i>Valete amici, quos amor</i></p>
    <p><i>Illius, heu, nimis tenet:</i></p>
    <p><i>Quos comparare grandibus</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Marginal "C" at top right and a fragment "Fa" at lower right are not text of the stanzas; a reference mark "C" is given as printed. Several letters are doubtful due to the scan, including "Prōtul", "alno", "sanguinem", "grandibus" and the final line; the scan is faint and some words may be misread. Marginal ink specks and show-through were disregarded.</notes>
